  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "A calmer rental workspace",
    "overview": "Trozy's implemented interface uses fresh light-pink fills, white work surfaces and readable dark-pink labels for actions and current selection. The visual direction supports everyday Vietnamese rental-management tasks through readable hierarchy, consistent controls and clear separation between information and decisions.\n\nThe system is restrained and practical. A content-sized property selector in the topbar and a primary navigation bar that groups trailing destinations into Thêm (n) when space is limited handle frequent tasks, while the supplementary sidebar uses three accordion groups plus utility links and can become a compact rail or overlay drawer. The topbar and primary navigation hide together after 24px of downward travel beyond 140px of page scroll and reveal after 12px upward; open drawer/property-picker/search/More-menu/logout states and keyboard focus keep them available. Focus or route/property/user changes reveal the header, reduced-motion settings suppress its transition, and tables and forms adapt structurally to the available width. Original meter images and verification controls remain operational content rather than decoration.\n\nThe content-sized property combobox keeps its closed trigger compact with the workspace caption and selected name. Addresses appear only after expanding its listbox, beneath each individual active property name. There is no all-properties option. A per-account preference restores a valid selection; missing or archived IDs fall back before content renders, and an empty active set produces an operational empty state. Names and addresses truncate inside the available width, with full text available in titles and accessible descriptions. Pale fills use the separate primary-foreground token; links and selected labels use accent-text, and visible control outlines use focus. Rendered browser QA is not claimed. The Trozy wordmark starts with an uppercase T. A continuous 2px fresh-pink divider separates the primary navigation from content. The dashboard opens with the current weekday/date and preserved task buttons, without greetings or a question banner. Room management defaults to a property/floor-grouped summary table with a separate individual-room tab. Shared filters also scope its landlord XLSX download. Current-lease and actual reservation deposits are kept separate, issued invoice debt is labelled per room, and only confirmed utility readings enter the overview. The primary bar measures actual container and active-label widths, keeping the leading routes that fit and exposing the remainder through a keyboard-accessible Thêm menu. A hidden current route highlights its trigger; outside focus, resizing and route/property/account changes dismiss the popup with focus recovery. Inert zero-size measurement spans avoid duplicate controls, and observers plus font-loading events keep the split current. Color roles now separate a neutral gray work canvas and dark ink from light-pink outlined actions. Solid teal cash/occupied, blue vacant/water and amber maintenance/electric series retain written labels and exact values. Room badges and card backgrounds use the same status families. Focus and interactive boundaries use dedicated contrast-tested tokens; utility history no longer fades older periods. Manual meter entry explicitly distinguishes cumulative start/end readings from period consumption. The optional consumption method shows read-only cumulative starts and calculated ends, preserves a valid interval when switching methods, and still requires owner evidence comparison and confirmation. Smaller monthly usage is allowed without changing the canonical cumulative API, historical readings or tenant photo-only workflow. Property selection also scopes notification/maintenance counters and tenant dashboard deposits. The picker supports keyboard navigation and explicit header visibility locking, closes on outside interaction or resizing and clamps its popup inside the viewport. Landlords can create properties through a header plus button or open property management from the selector footer. A single dialog supports listing, editing, opening, archive/restore and explicitly confirmed deletion. New properties are selected after refreshed data contains the returned ID. Pending work prevents repeated requests; errors retain input. Server deletion allows only truly empty properties, blocks linked business records and uploaded files, removes only the empty property configuration and retains audit history. Tenant views omit management actions; archive retains the existing active-contract guard.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
